<http://data.silknow.org/object/6058371a-8ce2-3c8a-a252-3963d82070d6/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Textile panel of crimson silk damask. With a symmetrical design of thick knobbly branches meandering from the side to the centre where they are joined by a scalloped ring. From these branches spring large leaves, flowers and fruit and some have decorative fillings. The satin is a satin of 5. There is no repeat in the height of the silk. The width is the complete loom width, and an applied trimming of gold braid covers the selvedges. These are approximately 0.375 inch wide with satin stripes of green and white edge by seven red silk cords."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6058371a-8ce2-3c8a-a252-3963d82070d6> .

